A||||5||2farnorth||Fuel pump keeps running||||9||
Z||000000||2farnorth||10-02-2001||06:16 AM||||I have an 85 SE v6 that the fuel pump keeps running when the key is off.  I unplugged the relay and nothing changed.  Had to pull the fuel pump fuse to keep it from running the battery down again.  Could the oil pressure sending unit cause this ?<P>Thanks<P>Dave||||reg||9
Z||000001||Dan87GT||10-02-2001||07:23 AM||||It is the oil pressure sender. I had this happen to me a few years ago, kept pulling the fuse when I stopped. The oil pressure sender has a safety wired in, it will cut the fuel pressure if the oil pressure goes away. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-02-2001||07:35 AM||||I agree with Dan87GT, oil pressure sending unit shorting out. Replaced unit, problem went away.  Insure that the wiring plug has the rubber grommet protecting the plug connector from water.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black86SE||10-02-2001||06:18 PM||||I have just the oppisite problem. When I turn my key on, to the run position, nothing happens. No fuel pump sound or anything. Then it takes a good 5-10 seconds of turning over to get it started. Usually. Sometimes if I start it soon after parking it and it is on level ground, it will start instantly.<P>------------------<BR>1986 V6 SE<BR>Black<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||10-02-2001||07:16 PM||||Pump run on is oil pressure switch stuck closed.<P>Long crank is fuel pump relay. Cranking brings up the oil pressure which closes the switch and powers the fuel pump.||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||10-02-2001||09:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B><BR>Long crank is fuel pump relay. Cranking brings up the oil pressure which closes the switch and powers the fuel pump.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Cool, I didnt know that. That is very helpful for me w/ the probs Im having w/ my Formula...thanx terryk!<BR>BTW, for the original question, yes it is the oil sending unit....cheap part and EXTREMELY easy fix (5 minute).<P><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
